      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2010 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "A coronary artery aneurysm (CAA), the etiology and treatment of which are still not fully understood, is uncommonly encountered. A giant CAA is extremely rare and only a limited number of cases have been reported. We report the case of a 37-year-old female with a giant right coronary artery aneurysm that was successfully treated by surgical excision."
      },
